            <div xml:id="d1394">

                <pb facs="0925" n="809" xml:id="pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/258.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I beg to inform you that
                    I received a telegram last night from Sr. Joaquin Armendaiz, who is now at
                    Alpine, Texas, in which he states that the Constitutionalists at Monterey have
                    demanded 40,000 pesos from him as a payment to avoid the confiscation of his
                    property. It is absolutely impossible for him to pay this sum and he asks me to
                    appeal to you for protection.</p>
                <p>Sr. Armendaiz has never taken any part in the politics of Mexico; he has already
                    suffered greatly in his interests at the hands of the Constitutionalists, and if
                    this last demand is enforced, it means financial ruin to him.</p>
                <p>I beg you therefore to interpose your good offices on his behalf, and to make the
                    necessary representations to the Constitutionalists, in order to prevent the
                    confiscation of the property of my compatriot.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
